Bug 624082 - Do not lose moved messages when a playback run decides from a stale list that a folder is done. r=BenC,tobyp

Moving messages between two folders of the same IMAP account can lose them: they
disappear from both folders in the client while they are still sitting in the
source folder on the server.

`nsImapOfflineSync` decided a folder had nothing left from the list of pending
operations it reads once, when it opens the folder's database, and cleared
`nsMsgFolderFlags::OfflineEvents`. That list cannot carry the decision. It does
not hold operations recorded after it was read, and a run that gives up on a
folder early leaves behind ones it never tried. Playback opens a folder's
database only when that flag is set, so whatever was left could never run again.

Ask the database instead, wherever the run is finished with it. When it cannot be
asked the flag is cleared as before, because `UpdateFolder` starts playback
instead of selecting a folder whose flag is set.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318396

diff --git a/mailnews/imap/src/nsImapOfflineSync.cpp b/mailnews/imap/src/nsImapOfflineSync.cpp
--- a/mailnews/imap/src/nsImapOfflineSync.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/imap/src/nsImapOfflineSync.cpp
@@ -21,8 +21,28 @@
 #include "nsMsgUtils.h"
 #include "nsIAutoSyncManager.h"
 #include "mozilla/Components.h"
 
+/**
+ * Set or clear the `nsMsgFolderFlags::OfflineEvents` flag on `folder`,
+ * depending on whether it has any offline operations queued in its database.
+ * Call this while that database is still open. Special case: if the database
+ * cannot be asked, the flag is cleared.
+ */
+static void UpdateOfflineEventsFlag(nsIMsgFolder* folder,
+                                    nsIMsgOfflineOpsDatabase* db) {
+  MOZ_ASSERT(folder);
+  nsTArray<nsMsgKey> pending;
+  if (db && NS_SUCCEEDED(db->ListAllOfflineOpIds(pending)) &&
+      !pending.IsEmpty()) {
+    folder->SetFlag(nsMsgFolderFlags::OfflineEvents);
+  } else {
+    // UpdateFolder hands a folder whose flag is set to the playback machinery
+    // instead of selecting it, so a flag we cannot justify has to go.
+    folder->ClearFlag(nsMsgFolderFlags::OfflineEvents);
+  }
+}
+
